{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A song of ascents. Behold, bless</b> — Behold, since you shall be like the dew of Hermon, blessed, behold you are obligated to bless HaShem." "And the sense of <b>by night</b> — that you shall bless Him also by nights, for the good things He did with you. And it speaks to the priests, therefore —"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 134, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:40.376357486Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}